  "worked_solution": "A function $f(x)$ is concave up over an interval $(a,b)$ if ${f}^{\u2033}(x)>0$ for all $x\\in (a,b).$\n\nOn the given graph of $y={f}^{\u2033}(x),$ we can see that ${f}^{\u2033}(x)>0$ on the intervals  $(-1,0)$ and  $(0,1).$  Therefore, the function $f(x)$ is concave up on the intervals  $(-1,0)$ and  $(0,1).$",
